      <div class="yeast-screen__inner yeast-screen--reverse">
        <div class="yeast-screen__content">
          <!-- 2026-10-21（用户提供英文正文，逐字照录）：整屏改为「左标题 + 右侧四段」。
               左栏自上而下：Future Vision 字图眉标 → 主标题 → 导语 → 页底总结句（细线分隔）；
               右栏：四段纵向排列，段首细线 + 序号 01–04。
               原「五模块」四宫格与副题胶囊字图（From H1N1 to the Broad Spectrum Platform）
               随新文本撤下；本屏只描述愿景与后续验证需求，不声称任何检测性能。 -->
          <h2 class="sr-only">Future Vision: From Modular Research to Shared Public Health Value</h2>
          <div class="fv-split">
            <div class="fv-lead">
              <img fetchpriority="low" loading="lazy" class="fv-title-img reveal" src="{{ basePath | default('') }}static/image/home/09-future-vision-title.png"
                alt="Future Vision" width="1056" height="529" decoding="async">
              <h2 class="fv-headline reveal">From Modular Research to Shared Public Health Value</h2>
              <p class="fv-deck reveal">EchoYeast’s contribution goes beyond the pursuit of a single biosensor.
                By sharing characterized reporter parts, yeast-engineering evidence, computational hypotheses,
                and the lessons from designs that did not yet work, we aim to give future teams a clearer
                starting point. Our long-term vision is to explore how modular living-cell sensing could support
                environmental monitoring—through open research, careful validation, and responsible design.</p>
              <div class="fv-closing reveal">
                <p class="fv-closing__line">Our contribution today is a documented foundation for further research.</p>
                <p class="fv-closing__line fv-closing__line--strong">Our vision for tomorrow is more accessible,
                  evidence-based environmental monitoring.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <ol class="fv-list">
              <li class="fv-item reveal">
                <span class="fv-item__num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
                <div class="fv-item__text">
                  <h3 class="fv-item__title">Reusable Knowledge for Future Teams</h3>
                  <p class="fv-item__body">We contribute <i>FUS1</i>-based reporter parts, yeast-editing
                    components, and documentation of Gpa1 C-terminal engineering. Together with construction
                    records and characterization results, these resources provide starting points for future
                    yeast-biosensor projects. Clearly distinguishing demonstrated results from unresolved
                    questions helps others assess what can be reused and what still requires validation.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="fv-item reveal">
                <span class="fv-item__num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
                <div class="fv-item__text">
                  <h3 class="fv-item__title">A Future Role in Environmental Monitoring</h3>
                  <p class="fv-item__body">Our long-term goal is to explore whether yeast-based sensing could
                    complement existing approaches to monitoring influenza-related environmental signals. Such a
                    system would not replace clinical testing or determine whether an individual is infected.
                    Any future application would require evidence of specificity, sensitivity, reliability, and
                    performance in relevant sample conditions.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="fv-item reveal">
                <span class="fv-item__num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
                <div class="fv-item__text">
                  <h3 class="fv-item__title">Accessibility as a Design Goal</h3>
                  <p class="fv-item__body">Our temperature-controlled optical-readout prototype allows us to
                    explore how biological sensing might be paired with accessible instrumentation.
                    Affordability, ease of operation, maintenance, and local resource needs remain design
                    priorities rather than demonstrated advantages. Their practical value must be assessed
                    alongside biological performance.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="fv-item reveal">
                <span class="fv-item__num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
                <div class="fv-item__text">
                  <h3 class="fv-item__title">Open Development, Responsible Progress</h3>
                  <p class="fv-item__body">We aim to share not only successful modules, but also
                    limitations—including unresolved full-length receptor expression and HA-dependent
                    activation. Future work must address biological containment, sample handling, and the
                    interpretation of results. By making both progress and uncertainty visible, EchoYeast seeks
                    to support more transparent and responsible biosensor development.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
